humb/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp/38px-Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp/50px-Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Stunned Condition Icon.webp\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div></td><td class=\"mbox-text\"><div class=\"mbox-text-span\">This is a disambiguation page, which links to ambiguously named articles. If you were <a href=\"/wiki/Special:WhatLinksHere/Soul\" title=\"Special:WhatLinksHere/Soul\">brought here</a> by a link in an article, consider editing it to direct towards the intended page instead.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Souls</b> are the animating spirits of living <a href=\"/wiki/Creatures\" title=\"Creatures\">creatures</a> in the world of Toril, the setting of <i>Baldur's Gate 3</i>. Soul can also refer to one of the following:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/True_Soul\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"True Soul\">True Soul</a>, high-ranking members of the <a href=\"/wiki/Cult_of_the_Absolute\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cult of the Absolute\">Cult of the Absolute</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Tormented_Soul\" title=\"Tormented Soul\">Tormented Soul</a>, a type of <a href=\"/wiki/Undead\" title=\"Undead\">Undead</a> creature.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Soul_Coin\" title=\"Soul Coin\">Soul Coin</a>, a miscellaneous item used to power the <a href=\"/wiki/Origins\" title=\"Origins\">origin</a> character <a href=\"/wiki/Karlach\" title=\"Karlach\">Karlach</a>'s infernal engine.</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260715165750\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\